ing this one out because of the  ingredients ginseng is their star  ingredient here they say they included  it because it's been shown to Target  wrinkles it is really popular in Korean  skincare there's also rationale with an  A and this is a stronger form of vitamin  A that converts to retinoic acid  tretinoin in just one step and so it is  as close to tretinoin as you can get in  a cosmetic product so it is one step  closer than retinol with an O vitamin A  derivatives retinoids are like the gold  standard ingredients in skin care and  retinelle with an A has been making its  way into a lot of skin care products  rationale is usually encapsulated in  products and this improves the stability  of it this is really good because  retinoids are kind of notoriously  unstable there was one study that looked  at how much retinol was left in a bunch  of different products and after six  months one of them had degraded by 80  percent encapsulation also means that  the rationale gets very gradually  released onto the skin you don't just  get one massive flood at the start and  so that usually gives you less  irritation but you can still get similar  overall results sometimes I have a  little bit of doubt about some forms of  encapsulation I'm not sure it's actually  releasing all of the retinoid out of the  capsule but I don't think it's a problem  for the main form on the market which is  cyclodextrin or what's used in this  which is liposomes the rationale is that  0.02 which I think is like a nice low to  medium intensity this is one of the most  inexpensive rationale products I've seen  and of course you don't have to just use  it around your eyes on the beauty of  chosen website they actually recommend  that you can use it on the rest of your  face and on other parts of your body too  so if you're looking for like a general  rationale product to try this one is a  really good option you might want to  look out for irritation though I saw  Kelly Driscoll mentioned that 